Dear Hiring Team,

I am pleased to apply for the *Early Career Technologist* position with *MetLife*. I bring more than three years of software engineering experience, a Master of Science in Computer Science from Pace University, and a record of developing and supporting full stack software applications that combine responsive user interfaces, secure APIs, data systems, and production AI capabilities.

At Sperse, I designed, tested, and deployed a React, TypeScript, Python, and FastAPI workflow platform serving more than 10,000 users. I integrated GenAI APIs, prompt engineering, LangChain, and LlamaIndex into a system that routes requests across 40+ specialized agents with validated tool calls and tenant-aware access control. I also built CI/CD pipelines with automated testing and trace-based evaluations to catch latency, accuracy, and safety issues before deployment. This work directly prepares me to help MetLife deliver scalable, secure, and intelligent full stack solutions while responsibly integrating AI capabilities into applications.

My experience also reflects the operational and collaborative responsibilities of this role. At Sperse, I gathered and refined product requirements and user stories with cross-functional teams, participated in peer reviews of code and solution designs, and added Redis-backed observability to resolve production incidents and service requests. At Qualitest, I developed a cloud-native Java and Spring Boot service spanning AWS S3, Google Cloud Storage, PostgreSQL, and Redis, then improved error recovery across more than 100,000 weekly AWS Step Functions and Lambda executions. These accomplishments required strong communication, disciplined problem-solving, and the ability to learn and apply new technologies quickly in Agile environments.

MetLife's purpose—always being with people while building a more confident future—strongly resonates with me. I am especially drawn to the values *Win Together* and *Think Ahead*: they reflect how I collaborate across functions and use contemporary engineering and AI tools to anticipate reliability, security, and customer needs. I would welcome the opportunity to contribute those strengths to Global Technology and help simplify complex processes, improve technology resiliency, and create trustworthy experiences for MetLife's customers. I can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration.

